From: gsm-system folk/uhd4
Subject: [PATCH] CommonLibs: don't redefine gettid() on glibc >= 2.30
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026

glibc 2.30 added gettid() to <unistd.h>. The old
"#if !defined(gettid)" guard only detects macros, so on new glibc
it defines a colliding gettid() macro and the build dies with:
  error: macro "gettid" passed 1 arguments, but takes just 0
Skip the fallback where the C library already provides gettid();
call sites keep working (same thread-ID semantics).

--- a/CommonLibs/Logger.h
+++ b/CommonLibs/Logger.h
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 // If timestr decl is changed G++ will whine when Utils.h is included.
 namespace Utils { const std::string timestr(); };

-#if !defined(gettid)
+#if !defined(gettid) && !__GLIBC_PREREQ(2,30)
 # define gettid() syscall(SYS_gettid)
 #endif // !defined(gettid)

--- a/CommonLibs/Threads.cpp
+++ b/CommonLibs/Threads.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 int gMutexLogLevel = LOG_INFO;	// The mutexes cannot call gConfig or gGetLoggingLevel so we have to get the log level indirectly.

-#if !defined(gettid)
+#if !defined(gettid) && !__GLIBC_PREREQ(2,30)
 # define gettid() syscall(SYS_gettid)
 #endif // !defined(gettid)
